statement: Reachable-row transition synthesis bound. Let D be a set of r distinct reachable input rows in {0,1}^k and T:D→{0,1}^w any transition map. In the basis fan-in-two AND/OR gates with free NOT, constants, and unrestricted fan-out, T can be implemented on D using at most r(k−1)+w·max(r−1,0) counted gates. Proof: For each z∈D form its equality indicator δ_z as the conjunction of its k literals; a k-input conjunction takes k−1 fan-in-two AND gates (for k=0 use the sole empty row and its indicator is constant 1). On D these indicators are one-hot. For each output coordinate j, OR the indicators whose T(z)_j=1, using at most max(r−1,0) OR gates; if the set is empty use constant 0. This agrees with T on D. Summing gives the bound. For k=S+1 transition inputs and w=S state bits this is rS+S·max(r−1,0), with no requirement on behavior outside D.
scope: Exact finite synthesis upper bound for arbitrary maps on a specified reachable domain; free NOT and constants, fan-in-two AND/OR, unrestricted fan-out. This is a reusable upper bound, not an optimality claim or P vs NP result.
